  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nx = 4 + √15\n\n**Formula used:**\n\n(a + b)² = a² + b² + 2ab\n\n(a + b) (a - b) = a² - b²\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nx = 4 + √15\n\nSo, 1/x = 1/(4 + √15)\n\n= (4 - √15)/[(4 + √15) (4 - √15)]\n\n= (4 - √15)/(16 - 15)\n\n= 4 - √15\n\nThen, x + (1/x) = (4 + √15) + (4 - √15)\n\n⇒ x + (1/x) = 8\n\n⇒ [x + (1/x)]² = 8² [Taking square on both sides]\n\n⇒ x² + (1/x²) + [2 × x × (1/x)] = 64\n\n⇒ x2 + (1/x2) + 2 = 64\n\n⇒ x2 + (1/x2) = 64 - 2 = 62\n\n**∴ The value of x2 + (1/x2) is 62**",
